{"text":"Dashboard write-API request-safety trio (Fastify 5, browser-only same-origin surface, no auth tokens, no CORS). Every write endpoint: (1) require Content-Type: application/json else 415; (2) fail-closed same-origin check — reject unless Sec-Fetch-Site is same-origin OR Origin matches the host, else 403; (3) 64KB bodyLimit else 413; (4) never add @fastify/cors. Routing: a method-guard onRequest hook with an EXACT-match allow-list (not a path prefix) — trailing slash, query string, extra segment and case variants must all 405. See packages/server/src/plugins/method-guard.ts + routes/rating-write.ts.","tags":["security","fastify","write-api","csrf","sessions-spike-v4","patterns"],"recorded_at":"2026-05-18","applies_to":"metaswarm-dashboard"}
{"text":"Filesystem reads of user-controlled paths (URL params, transcript directory names): sanitize each path segment against ^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$ and reject any '..'; refuse symlinks via lstat (not stat); then realpath the resolved path and assert it is contained within the expected root directory before opening it. Defends transcript discovery (reads ~/.claude/projects) and the rating read/write routes (the datalake) against path traversal + symlink escape. See packages/sessions/src/transcript-discovery.ts.","tags":["security","filesystem","path-traversal","symlink","sessions-spike-v4","patterns"],"recorded_at":"2026-05-18","applies_to":"metaswarm-dashboard"}
